  "findings": [
    "Initial constructor index traverses original prior order; general declaration index remains reversed unchanged.",
    "Tail-first, then all children, then Ctr-head insertion gives existing first depth-first winner for each exact name, including duplicate child/head/sibling cases.",
    "Non-Ctr nodes do not occupy constructor entries but their children remain traversed.",
    "Miss adapter returns historical f_find(name,Nil), preserving Missing tag and query spelling.",
    "f_context_declared receives qualified header; incremental index update agrees with prepending that header. Ordinary/partialADT nodes without children return identical ctor tree.",
    "Constructor accumulation remains local until existing final ADT publication; partial constructors gain no early visibility.",
    "Five scoped lookup expressions changed; all local/raw lookups remain unchanged.",
    "Builder traverses completed declaration and child metadata once, never term types or bodies. It intentionally does not promise raw early-exit poison-tail behavior during index construction.",
    "Existing raw34 is retained but cannot alone validate new index. Separate factory/find/incremental/persistence/collision controls and public affected tests are required before cost/promotion."
  ],
  "limits": "Source review only. Finite index controls, checked build, broad integration and performance decisions remain separate. No compiler edits or profile/probe jobs performed by reviewer.",
